# Line endings: LF everywhere, all platforms.
# text=auto + eol=lf makes Git normalize any CRLF (e.g. files saved by Windows
# editors) back to LF at add time and check out LF, so the index always holds
# LF and a Windows-side save produces a clean, single-line diff instead of a
# whole-file rewrite. Text parsers in the build chain (tsc, vitest, rustc,
# PowerShell, YAML/JSON, NSIS) are CRLF/LF-agnostic — this exists to keep
# history readable, not to fix builds.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats — Git must never touch or normalize these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.node  binary
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary
.DS_Store binary
